 "finish_summary": "I characterized the timing budget first: a logic-free version (y_o <= a_i) reaches WNS 7.888 ns, so the entire 32-bit adder plus enable/reset logic only costs ~0.32 ns (~5-6 cell levels), while area is worth only 0.001 pt/um^2 versus 10 pt/ns. I then probed many adder architectures with estimate_ppa: Kogge-Stone (7.499), Sklansky (7.507), Han-Carlson (7.404), Sklansky/KS with OR-propagate (7.512/7.501), carry-select 2x16 and 4x8 (7.393/7.260), explicit ripple (5.683), subtract-form add (7.510), plus restructurings that pull the synchronous reset and the valid enable off the sum path and even select the flop data with the carry (7.487-7.560). Every alternative was slower than the flow's native `+` mapping (7.5707 ns, 671 um^2), and the area savings (up to 150 um^2 = 0.15 pt) never compensated the 0.05-0.3 ns timing loss (0.5-3 pt). The native mapping is therefore already at the depth limit for Nangate45 here, and I submitted it to place-and-route, verifying a score of 74.156 (area 746.13 um^2, WNS 7.49026 ns). Three P&R submissions were left unused because no candidate had a credible chance of beating it.",
